  "answer": "Tooth decay starts when the pH of the mouth is lower than 5.5 because tooth enamel, which is made of calcium phosphate, begins to corrode under acidic conditions. Bacteria in the mouth produce acids by breaking down sugar and food particles, which lowers the pH. When the pH drops below 5.5, the enamel starts to dissolve, leading to tooth decay. Using basic toothpaste can neutralize the acid and prevent this process.",
